{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1090637-bale-hounds-and-norse-myths","id":1090637,"title":"Bale Hounds and Norse Myths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-10T01:36:42-07:00","id":1090637,"title":"Bale Hounds and Norse Myths","content":"Hammering my Uppsala game, I think about main antagonist of the chronicle. On general they are Bale Hounds, in all possible Tribes ( Pure also ), that survived inside local population. But main character will be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1089754-2e-wta-tribe-as-wtf-lodge-%E2%80%93-black-spiral-dancers\">Black Spiral Dancer</a> that corrupted latest Packs generation. As main theme of chronicle are Norse Myths, I thinking how to marry Bale Hounds philosophy with ideas from Northman Mythology.<br /> <br /> Obvious one is using Ragnarok, as Apocalypse-like event Norse Bale Hounds want to create. The problem, I got, is that Ragnarok is much more 'god driven', at least according to myths. <b>How would Norse Bale Hounds approach this kind of thing?</b><br /> <br /> Bonus question - I look for some nice 'wicked' <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_kennings\" target=\"_blank\">Kenning</a> to make Deed Name for this character, but does not seems to find anything working. Got some unsettling propositions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T02:07:32-07:00","id":1090644,"title":"","content":"When Christianity first spread to the Norse, how was the idea of the Devil translated? That might be where you need to look. Hel, Nidhoggr, and Surtr will probably come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T03:01:49-07:00","id":1090659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1090637-bale-hounds-and-norse-myths?p=1090644#post1090644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Christianity first spread to the Norse, how was the idea of the Devil translated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to dwell into that in Viking Era part of chronicle, but I assumed for now that Maeljin become 'Devils Legion'/'Princes of Hell', with Asmodai as Satan himself, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1090637-bale-hounds-and-norse-myths?p=1090644#post1090644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be where you need to look. Hel, Nidhoggr, and Surtr will probably come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was aiming for male antagonist, but when you mentioned Hel, I got now nice feeling about female Uratha that was casted out by Forsaken decades ago, now with half face marred with scars, that as Daughter of Loki want's to bring Ragnarok in his name, commiting to Maeljins for help. Only some evil sounding Kenning on her, and I think I got my main villian, thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T03:23:47-07:00","id":1090665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1090637-bale-hounds-and-norse-myths?p=1090659#post1090659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was aiming for male antagonist, but when you mentioned Hel, I got now nice feeling about female Uratha that was casted out by Forsaken decades ago, now with half face marred with scars, that as Daughter of Loki want's to bring Ragnarok in his name, commiting to Maeljins for help. Only some evil sounding Kenning on her, and I think I got my main villian, thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked it. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hel_(being)#Seo_Hell\" target=\"_blank\">Another thing on Wikipedia</a> that you might be interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T04:12:59-07:00"